From 986eebecf98fb7a2bed3360003959e5201743bbe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 14:01:39 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] mt-http-resolver: tenant-resolver middleware +
 /api/platform/tenants + VK bearer auth
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

HTTP-edge half of the multi-tenant story. After this patch any request
carrying `x-f5xc-tenant: acme` becomes tenant-aware end-to-end via the
GORM callback (patch2) — no per-handler edits required to make the
existing /api/governance/virtual-keys, /api/providers, /api/mcp/clients,
etc. handlers tenant-scoped.

* handlers/tenant_resolver.go (new) — TenantResolverMiddleware peeks
  the `x-f5xc-tenant` header and stashes the value on the fasthttp
  UserValue + any pre-attached BifrostContext. When the
  BIFROST_DISABLE_DEFAULT_TENANT_CONFIG flag is on, any POST/PUT/PATCH/
  DELETE targeting the `default` tenant on an /api/<entity>/... path
  gets 403'd at ingress. /api/platform/* and /v1/* are intentionally
  excluded — operators sitting on default must be able to create their
  first real tenant via /api/platform/tenants, and inference policy
  lives in the governance plugin downstream.

* handlers/platform_tenants.go (new) — /api/platform/tenants CRUD for
  cross-tenant tenant-directory management. The ONE admin surface that
  is NOT per-tenant-scoped (the tenants table has no tenant_id column,
  so the GORM callback is a no-op here). When disableDefaultTenant is
  true, the seeded `default` tenant is hidden from list / get /
  update / delete responses.

* handlers/middlewares.go — auth middleware recognises the Bifrost VK
  prefix (sk-bf-…) as a valid bearer credential format and lets the
  request through. Governance plugin downstream remains the
  authoritative validator (active/inactive, scope, allowed_models,
  budget). Without this, a VK-only client (opencode, curl, an SDK)
  could not talk to /v1 when DisableAuthOnInference is false because
  validateSession would 401 on a non-session token.

* server/server.go — wires TenantResolverMiddleware into both the
  inference (/v1/*) and admin (/api/*) chains, instantiates
  NewPlatformTenantsHandler with the disable-default flag, and adds an
  envBool helper that gates BIFROST_DISABLE_DEFAULT_TENANT_CONFIG
  without pulling a flag library.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
